        "original_id": "8194e577-bcc0-573a-abd3-9faaccd8291d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Works: Jerk (play), Jerk (1993 novel)\n- People: Dennis Cooper, Gisèle Vienne, Jonathan Capdevielle, Dean Arnold Corll, David Brooks, Elmer Wayne Henley, Jr.\n- Roles: writer, director, performer, serial killer, accomplices\n- Places: Houston, Texas\n- Topics: murder cases, theatrical adaptation\n\nFacts:\n- Dean Arnold Corll was born on December 24, 1939.\n- Dennis Cooper wrote the 1993 novel Jerk.\n- From 1970 to 1973 in Houston, Texas, Dean Arnold Corll and his teenaged accomplices David Brooks and Elmer Wayne Henley, Jr. abducted, raped, tortured, and murdered at least 28 boys.\n- Dean Arnold Corll was an American serial killer.\n- Dean Arnold Corll died on August 8, 1973.\n- Jerk is a one-person puppet play by the American writer Dennis Cooper.\n- The play Jerk was made in collaboration with director Gisèle Vienne and performer Jonathan Capdevielle.\n- The play Jerk is based on Dennis Cooper's 1993 novel of the same name.",
